                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "49b3df4d-7aa5-3fe7-bbc8-09bcc338ff2a",
                        "entry_id": "c67f7bb8-8799-3c66-aeff-22f48de16293",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A major administrative subdivision of the Russian Empire; a governorate or province."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ecabe2b5-e3fb-4eec-9f72-2a39efee5303",
                                "sense_id": "49b3df4d-7aa5-3fe7-bbc8-09bcc338ff2a",
                                "text": "Milyukov’s density figure for the southeastern portion of Peter’s realm, referred to in his text as “the Kazan’ and Astrakhan’ gubernii” of that time, appears to be erroneous. It corresponds to the enumerated number of males in these two old gubernii, but the Nizhegorod Guberniya had been formed from parts of these gubernii during Peter’s reign and its area is definitely included in this region by Milyukov."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "09ac37de-233a-45af-9ebb-3854aba2f60e",
                                "sense_id": "49b3df4d-7aa5-3fe7-bbc8-09bcc338ff2a",
                                "text": "In the 1896–1900 period fertility and mortality were still moderately high, although significantly lower than in the Russian gubernii, in Kovno Guberniya, which occupied much of present-day Lithuania."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0fc6619-e827-46b0-b052-50aa4e532468",
                                "sense_id": "49b3df4d-7aa5-3fe7-bbc8-09bcc338ff2a",
                                "text": "According to official figures, in 1910 the proportion of new inhabitants acquiring land in Tobolsk and Tomsk gubernii who wished to resettle in other regions was between 5 and 6 per cent, and in Yeniseisk guberniya, 12.6 per cent."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cb773c4-4415-4304-83bf-1e56d0ee59b2",
                                "sense_id": "49b3df4d-7aa5-3fe7-bbc8-09bcc338ff2a",
                                "text": "Modern Lithuania consists of the Kovno guberniya, and half of Vilno and half of Suwalki (Polish) gubernii."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "678fe89b-b635-4a5b-be94-47c81e5d7933",
                        "source_entry_id": "c67f7bb8-8799-3c66-aeff-22f48de16293",
